WEBVTT

00:00:03.327 --> 00:00:13.171
The Wind in the Willows by Kenneth Graham.

00:00:13.231 --> 00:00:29.908
Chapter 1 The Riverbank It is spring, and the mould is cleaning his little home.

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:34.548
He is working very hard and he is very tired.

00:00:34.608 --> 00:00:38.219
Suddenly he decides to stop.

00:00:38.279 --> 00:00:40.940
He wants to go outside.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.271
He goes up a small tunnel and arrives outside in a meadow.

00:00:48.332 --> 00:00:53.903
He thinks when he arrives in the sunlight.

00:00:53.963 --> 00:00:56.934
This is better than cleaning."

00:00:56.994 --> 00:00:59.296
He is very happy.

00:00:59.356 --> 00:01:02.288
He crosses meadows and woods.

00:01:02.348 --> 00:01:06.990
He sees rabbits, birds and a lot of other animals.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.952
They are all working hard.

00:01:10.012 --> 00:01:13.284
Finally he arrives at the river.

00:01:13.344 --> 00:01:16.355
He sits down on the grass.

00:01:16.415 --> 00:01:20.517
The water rad comes out of his hole in the riverbank.

00:01:20.577 --> 00:01:22.264
He sees moles.

00:01:22.324 --> 00:01:24.392
Hello, Mole," he says.

00:01:24.452 --> 00:01:25.912
Would you like to come over?

00:01:25.972 --> 00:01:27.603
Oh, hello, Rat.

00:01:27.663 --> 00:01:28.824
Yes, I would.

00:01:28.884 --> 00:01:29.874
But how?

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:31.344
replies Mole.

00:01:31.404 --> 00:01:33.826
I can come and get you in my boat.

00:01:33.886 --> 00:01:38.258
Rat gets into a little boat and crosses the river.

00:01:38.318 --> 00:01:41.048
Mole gets into the boat.

00:01:41.108 --> 00:01:43.980
This is wonderful.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.750
Says Mole.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.822
This is my first time in a boat.

00:01:48.882 --> 00:01:51.368
Your first time says Rat.

00:01:51.428 --> 00:01:53.934
There's nothing better than boats.

00:01:53.994 --> 00:01:55.736
Let's go for a picnic.

00:01:55.795 --> 00:01:58.338
Oh, yes, please!

00:01:58.398 --> 00:01:59.969
says Mole.

00:02:00.029 --> 00:02:06.205
Rat goes into his house and returns with a big basket full of food.

00:02:06.264 --> 00:02:09.518
They go down the river in the boat.

00:02:09.577 --> 00:02:18.762
Rat tells Mole about life on the river and about his neighbours, the otters, kingfishers and moorhens.

00:02:18.822 --> 00:02:22.501
Mole sees a wood in the distance.

00:02:22.561 --> 00:02:24.592
What's over there?

00:02:24.652 --> 00:02:25.703
He asks.

00:02:25.763 --> 00:02:28.826
That's the wild wood, says Rat.

00:02:28.886 --> 00:02:31.076
We don't go there often.

00:02:31.136 --> 00:02:33.408
Are they nice people there?

00:02:33.468 --> 00:02:34.719
asks Mole.

00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:37.160
Well, replies Rat.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:40.853
The squirrels and rabbits are all right, and there's Badger.

00:02:40.913 --> 00:02:42.024
He's nice.

00:02:42.084 --> 00:02:48.463
But the weasels, stoats and foxes, you must be careful with them.

00:02:48.523 --> 00:02:53.341
They stop for their picnic, and Mole unpacks the basket.

00:02:53.401 --> 00:02:56.082
Soon the Otter arrives.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.514
Hello, Otter, says Rat.

00:02:58.574 --> 00:03:00.776
This is my friend, Mr. Mole.

00:03:00.836 --> 00:03:04.658
Please, to meet you, says Otter to Mole.

00:03:04.718 --> 00:03:10.352
Suddenly the Badger appears, and Rat invites him to the picnic.

00:03:10.412 --> 00:03:14.444
But Badger turns around and goes away.

00:03:14.504 --> 00:03:17.645
Badger hates company, says Rat.

00:03:17.704 --> 00:03:20.455
We don't see him often, but look!

00:03:20.515 --> 00:03:23.197
There's toad on the river in his new boat!

00:03:23.257 --> 00:03:25.258
It's toad's new hobby!"

00:03:25.318 --> 00:03:26.379
says Otter.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.440
Yes, says Rat.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:32.103
First it was sailing, then it was house-boating.

00:03:32.163 --> 00:03:34.936
He changes hobby all the time.

00:03:34.996 --> 00:03:39.549
Rat waves to toad, but toad doesn't stop.

00:03:39.608 --> 00:03:43.286
Rat and Mole return to Rat's house in the boat.

00:03:43.346 --> 00:03:53.802
Rat invites Mole to stay with him, and Mole is very happy.

00:03:53.862 --> 00:04:12.386
Chapter 2 The Open Road One summer morning, Mole and Rat decide to visit Mr Toad.

00:04:12.445 --> 00:04:15.806
They get in the boat and go up the river.

00:04:15.866 --> 00:04:19.166
Toad's rich, you know," says Rad.

00:04:19.226 --> 00:04:21.757
"'Is Toad very nice?"

00:04:21.817 --> 00:04:22.747
asks Mole.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:25.367
"'Oh, yes," replies Rad.

00:04:25.387 --> 00:04:27.398
"'He's very nice.

00:04:27.458 --> 00:04:31.708
He isn't very intelligent, but we can't all be clever.

00:04:31.768 --> 00:04:37.930
And sometimes he's boastful and arrogant, but he's got some good qualities."

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:41.586
Soon they arrive at Toad Hall.

00:04:41.646 --> 00:04:44.204
They pass by a boating-house.

00:04:44.264 --> 00:04:46.426
It is full of boats.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:49.347
They are all out of the water.

00:04:49.407 --> 00:04:53.189
It seems that Toad isn't interested in boating anymore.

00:04:53.249 --> 00:04:57.272
I wonder what his new hobby is, says Rat.

00:04:57.332 --> 00:05:03.565
Rat and Mole get out of the boat and walk across the gardens of Toad Hall.

00:05:03.625 --> 00:05:06.406
They see Toad in the garden.

00:05:06.466 --> 00:05:09.352
He is looking at a big map.

00:05:09.412 --> 00:05:13.228
He is very pleased to see Rat and Mole.

00:05:13.288 --> 00:05:15.830
Hello Toad, says Rat.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.822
This is my friend Mole.

00:05:17.882 --> 00:05:19.464
Oh splendid!

00:05:19.524 --> 00:05:22.177
Christ Toad, pleased to meet you.

00:05:22.237 --> 00:05:24.339
Come and see my new hobby.

00:05:24.359 --> 00:05:28.202
He shows them a gypsy caravan.

00:05:28.262 --> 00:05:31.684
It is yellow and green with red wheels.

00:05:31.744 --> 00:05:35.526
There's real life, Christ Toad.

00:05:35.586 --> 00:05:41.850
The open road, travel, change, interest, excitement.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:45.522
Look inside, everything's there.

00:05:45.582 --> 00:05:48.984
We've got everything for our journey this afternoon.

00:05:49.044 --> 00:05:55.238
Excuse me, you say, we, our, this afternoon?

00:05:55.298 --> 00:05:56.610
Ask Rat.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:06:00.800
Yes, Ratty, I can't go without you, says Toad.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.810
Oh Rat, it's so exciting!

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.112
Says Mole.

00:06:05.172 --> 00:06:07.213
Very well, says Rat.

00:06:07.273 --> 00:06:08.694
Let's go!

00:06:08.754 --> 00:06:13.528
After lunch they go to the paddock and catch the old grey horse.

00:06:13.588 --> 00:06:16.410
Then they set off on the road.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:24.777
It is a lovely afternoon, and the birds whistle at them, and passersby say, Good afternoon!

00:06:24.797 --> 00:06:26.489
Good afternoon!

00:06:26.549 --> 00:06:30.828
In the evening they stop and eat a simple meal.

00:06:30.888 --> 00:06:33.444
Then they go to bed.

00:06:33.504 --> 00:06:40.308
The next morning Toad sleeps until very late, so Mole walks to the nearest village.

00:06:40.368 --> 00:06:48.182
He buys milk and eggs for breakfast, and rat lights a fire and washes the dinner plates from the night before.

00:06:48.242 --> 00:06:52.014
They are very tired after this hard work.

00:06:52.073 --> 00:06:54.885
Finally, Toad gets up.

00:06:54.945 --> 00:07:01.071
Ugh, life on the road is very easy, he says.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:04.166
After breakfast, they set off.

00:07:04.226 --> 00:07:11.685
They are walking along the road when suddenly a magnificent motor car drives past.

00:07:11.745 --> 00:07:21.917
The horse is frightened and pulls the caravan off the road into a ditch.

00:07:21.977 --> 00:07:26.030
The caravan is ruined.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.311
Rat is furious.

00:07:28.371 --> 00:07:29.732
You villains!

00:07:29.792 --> 00:07:30.722
Police!

00:07:30.782 --> 00:07:31.573
Help!

00:07:31.633 --> 00:07:32.844
He shouts.

00:07:32.904 --> 00:07:36.445
But Toad is sitting in the middle of the road.

00:07:36.505 --> 00:07:39.917
He is staring in the direction of the motor car.

00:07:39.977 --> 00:07:41.177
Poop, poop!

00:07:41.237 --> 00:07:42.208
He says.

00:07:42.268 --> 00:07:43.978
Poop, poop!

00:07:44.038 --> 00:07:49.402
Rat and Mole try to pull the caravan out of the ditch, but they can't.

00:07:49.462 --> 00:07:51.113
Rat asks.

00:07:51.173 --> 00:07:53.356
Can you help us, Toad?

00:07:53.416 --> 00:07:55.007
Boop, boop!

00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:56.929
Replies, Toad.

00:07:56.988 --> 00:08:02.843
Now that's the real way to travel, the only way.

00:08:02.903 --> 00:08:08.288
The caravan is ruined, and they must return home by train.

00:08:08.347 --> 00:08:19.243
The next day, Toad buys a big and very expensive motica.

00:08:19.303 --> 00:08:25.824
Chapter 3.

00:08:25.884 --> 00:08:33.366
The Wildwood.

00:08:33.427 --> 00:08:41.799
Mole wants to meet Badger.

00:08:41.859 --> 00:08:44.540
Could you ask him here for dinner?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.000
He asks Rat.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:47.320
He wouldn't come.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.761
Replies Rat.

00:08:48.821 --> 00:08:50.371
He hates company.

00:08:50.431 --> 00:08:53.150
Well, can we go and call on him?

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:54.889
suggests Smol.

00:08:54.949 --> 00:08:57.000
Oh no, says Rat.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:02.901
He's very shy, and also he lives in the middle of the Wildwood.

00:09:02.961 --> 00:09:07.392
It is clear that Rat doesn't want to visit Badger.

00:09:07.452 --> 00:09:12.052
It is wintertime, and Rat sleeps a lot.

00:09:12.112 --> 00:09:22.816
One afternoon, he is sleeping in his armchair in front of the fire, so Smol decides to go and explore the Wildwood and meet Badger.

00:09:22.876 --> 00:09:25.190
He goes outside.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:29.691
It is very cold, and the sky is grey.

00:09:29.751 --> 00:09:36.273
He is happy, and when he arrives at the Wildwood, he is not frightened.

00:09:36.333 --> 00:09:45.466
Then he starts to see faces, hundreds of faces, little faces with hard eyes.

00:09:45.526 --> 00:09:49.648
Mole is frightened and leaves the path.

00:09:49.708 --> 00:09:54.324
In a panic, Mole starts to run, he doesn't know where.

00:09:54.384 --> 00:09:59.109
Finally he hides inside the hollow of an old tree.

00:09:59.169 --> 00:10:02.983
Rat wakes up and looks for Mole.

00:10:03.044 --> 00:10:05.736
But Mole is not there.

00:10:05.796 --> 00:10:09.010
Mole's hat and boots are gone.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:12.358
Rat goes outside and sees footprints.

00:10:12.418 --> 00:10:16.094
They are going in the direction of the Wild Wood.

00:10:16.154 --> 00:10:18.256
Rat is worried.

00:10:18.316 --> 00:10:26.580
He goes back into the house, takes two pistols and a big stick, and sets off for the Wild Wood.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:35.236
He also sees little faces with hard eyes, but they disappear immediately when they see his pistols and stick.

00:10:35.296 --> 00:10:38.445
Rat hunts for an hour.

00:10:38.504 --> 00:10:41.542
Molly, Molly, where are you?

00:10:41.602 --> 00:10:44.052
It's me, Rat.

00:10:44.112 --> 00:10:47.763
Finally, he hears a cry.

00:10:47.823 --> 00:10:50.544
Ratty, is that really you?

00:10:50.604 --> 00:10:52.844
I'm so frightened.

00:10:52.904 --> 00:10:56.415
Rat sees Mole under the tree.

00:10:56.475 --> 00:11:00.336
Mole, you mustn't come into the Wildwood alone.

00:11:00.396 --> 00:11:04.007
We animals from the riverbank always come in couples.

00:11:04.067 --> 00:11:07.338
But brave Mr Toad isn't frightened of the wood.

00:11:07.398 --> 00:11:09.173
Says Mole.

00:11:09.233 --> 00:11:12.490
Rat laughs.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:13.460
Towed!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.773
He wouldn't come here for a hatful of gold!

00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:20.596
But now we must leave her home before night comes.

00:11:20.656 --> 00:11:22.908
Rat looks around.

00:11:22.968 --> 00:11:28.392
It's snowing, and everything looks so different in the snow.

00:11:28.452 --> 00:11:34.626
They set off bravely, but after two hours they stop for a rest.

00:11:34.686 --> 00:11:39.290
The snow is very deep, and they are very tired and wet.

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:42.763
We're very tired, says Rat.

00:11:42.823 --> 00:11:45.744
Let's find a dry cave or hole.

00:11:45.804 --> 00:11:49.466
Then we can rest before trying again.

00:11:49.526 --> 00:11:51.758
They look for shelter.

00:11:51.818 --> 00:11:54.229
Suddenly, Mole falls down.

00:11:54.249 --> 00:11:57.682
Oh, my leg!

00:11:57.742 --> 00:11:59.122
He cries.

00:11:59.182 --> 00:12:02.194
Poor Mole, says Rat.

00:12:02.254 --> 00:12:05.226
He looks at the cut on Mole's leg.

00:12:05.286 --> 00:12:09.390
This is a cut from metal, not a branch, he says.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:12.563
He starts to dig in the snow.

00:12:12.623 --> 00:12:13.763
Hooray!

00:12:13.783 --> 00:12:14.824
Hooray!

00:12:14.844 --> 00:12:16.114
He shouts.

00:12:16.174 --> 00:12:17.574
What is it?

00:12:17.634 --> 00:12:19.175
asks Mo.

00:12:19.235 --> 00:12:22.586
They see a little green door.

00:12:22.646 --> 00:12:25.617
A bell is hanging next to it.

00:12:25.677 --> 00:12:30.428
Under the bell is written, Mr. Badger.

00:12:30.488 --> 00:12:42.190
Rat hits the door with his stick, and Mo rings the bell.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:51.273
animals in winter.

00:12:51.333 --> 00:12:59.478
In winter time it gets cold, snow covers the ground and there is no food.

00:12:59.538 --> 00:13:03.420
So how do animals survive?

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.872
Migration.

00:13:05.932 --> 00:13:11.595
Many birds, fish and other animals migrate in the autumn.

00:13:11.655 --> 00:13:17.761
They travel south to warmer places and then return in the spring.

00:13:17.821 --> 00:13:20.325
adaptation.

00:13:20.385 --> 00:13:26.719
Some animals, like the mole, stay and remain active in the winter months.

00:13:26.778 --> 00:13:31.952
To keep warm they may grow new thicker fur in autumn.

00:13:32.012 --> 00:13:43.452
Because food is difficult to find, some animals like mice and squirrels collect extra food and store it to eat later.

00:13:43.512 --> 00:13:50.422
Some animals, such as the rat, hibernate during the winter.

00:13:50.483 --> 00:13:54.826
This is a special, very deep sleep.

00:13:54.886 --> 00:14:01.160
The animal's body temperature goes down, and its heartbeat and breathing slow down.

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:16.892
In the autumn, these animals prepare by eating extra food, which is stored as body fat, and can be used as energy during the winter.

00:14:16.952 --> 00:14:39.560
Chapter 4 Mr. Badger Mole and Rat wait for a long time and finally they hear footsteps.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:46.320
The door opens a little and they see a nose and two sleepy eyes.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.546
Who is it?

00:14:48.606 --> 00:14:50.028
asks Badger.

00:14:50.088 --> 00:14:52.180
He is angry.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.040
Oh, Badger.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.432
Cries, Rat.

00:14:55.492 --> 00:14:58.614
It's me, Rat, and my friend, Mole.

00:14:58.674 --> 00:15:00.586
We're lost in the snow.

00:15:00.646 --> 00:15:04.168
My dear Ratty, says Badger.

00:15:04.228 --> 00:15:09.162
Come in, lost in the snow, in the wild wood.

00:15:09.222 --> 00:15:13.846
This isn't the kind of night for small animals to be out.

00:15:13.906 --> 00:15:16.397
He takes them to the kitchen.

00:15:16.456 --> 00:15:19.518
There is a fire burning in the fireplace.

00:15:19.578 --> 00:15:23.262
Badger gives them dressing gowns and slippers.

00:15:23.322 --> 00:15:28.056
They sit in front of the fire while Badger prepares dinner for them.

00:15:28.116 --> 00:15:32.911
They are very hungry, and they eat and eat.

00:15:32.972 --> 00:15:35.624
How's old toad?

00:15:35.684 --> 00:15:37.146
asks Badger.

00:15:37.206 --> 00:15:40.444
From bad to worse, says Rat.

00:15:40.504 --> 00:15:43.140
Another accident in his car.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.690
This is the seventh.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.841
He's always in hospital or paying fines.

00:15:47.901 --> 00:15:52.712
He needs to pay for a driver, but he's convinced that he's a good driver.

00:15:52.772 --> 00:15:55.002
Badger thinks.

00:15:55.062 --> 00:16:01.464
I can't do anything now, but when the night's so short, we must talk to Toad.

00:16:01.524 --> 00:16:03.574
He must become sensible.

00:16:03.634 --> 00:16:07.005
Now, it's time for bed.

00:16:07.065 --> 00:16:09.600
He takes them to a room.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:16.347
It is full of food for the winter, apples, turnips, potatoes, nuts and honey.

00:16:16.407 --> 00:16:20.198
But there are also two little beds.

00:16:20.258 --> 00:16:25.180
Mole and rat get undressed and go to sleep.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:29.512
The next morning they get up very late.

00:16:29.572 --> 00:16:34.724
They are eating breakfast in the kitchen when the front doorbell rings.

00:16:34.784 --> 00:16:36.364
It's otter.

00:16:36.424 --> 00:16:39.958
He is very happy to see rat and mole.

00:16:40.018 --> 00:16:45.052
Everybody on the river is very worried about you, he says.

00:16:45.112 --> 00:16:48.683
At that moment, Badger arrives.

00:16:48.743 --> 00:16:51.284
I think it's time for lunch.

00:16:51.344 --> 00:16:52.774
He says.

00:16:52.834 --> 00:16:57.776
During lunch, Otter and Rad talk about the river.

00:16:57.836 --> 00:17:01.527
Mole tells Badger, I like your house.

00:17:01.587 --> 00:17:03.665
It's good to live underground.

00:17:03.725 --> 00:17:07.144
Badger is pleased that Mole likes his house.

00:17:07.204 --> 00:17:12.840
Yes, he reads safe, peaceful and quiet.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:17.234
After lunch, Badger shows Mole his home.

00:17:17.294 --> 00:17:20.636
There are a lot of rooms and tunnels.

00:17:20.696 --> 00:17:23.048
They return to the kitchen.

00:17:23.108 --> 00:17:25.520
Ratty is wearing his coat.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:28.813
Come on, Mole, it's time to go, he says.

00:17:28.873 --> 00:17:31.134
We must go before night.

00:17:31.194 --> 00:17:32.854
He is worried.

00:17:32.914 --> 00:17:35.343
It's all right, says Otter.

00:17:35.403 --> 00:17:36.743
I'm coming with you.

00:17:36.763 --> 00:17:39.594
Don't worry, Ratty.

00:17:39.654 --> 00:17:40.865
Says Badger.

00:17:40.925 --> 00:17:44.376
My tunnels go to the edge of the wood.

00:17:44.436 --> 00:17:49.847
He picks up a lantern and takes them down a long tunnel.

00:17:49.908 --> 00:17:53.579
After a long time, they see daylight.

00:17:53.639 --> 00:17:57.634
They are on the edge of the wild wood.

00:17:57.694 --> 00:18:02.410
Badger says goodbye, and goes away quickly.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.571
Otter takes them to the river.

00:18:05.631 --> 00:18:14.816
Mole is very happy to be home.

00:18:14.876 --> 00:18:22.160
Chapter 5.

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:31.384
Mr. Toad It is a sunny morning in summer.

00:18:31.444 --> 00:18:34.306
Mole and Rat are having breakfast.

00:18:34.366 --> 00:18:38.420
Suddenly, there is a knock at the door.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:43.164
Mole goes to the door and comes back with Badger.

00:18:43.224 --> 00:18:46.016
Badger looks very serious.

00:18:46.076 --> 00:18:47.426
It's time.

00:18:47.486 --> 00:18:49.958
He says, time for what?

00:18:50.019 --> 00:18:51.319
asks Rat.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.181
He looks at the clock.

00:18:53.241 --> 00:18:54.772
Time for who?

00:18:54.832 --> 00:18:55.998
Says Badger.

00:18:56.058 --> 00:18:58.214
Time for Toad.

00:18:58.274 --> 00:19:00.175
We must talk to him.

00:19:00.235 --> 00:19:05.577
I know that another big new motor car is arriving at Toad Hall today.

00:19:05.637 --> 00:19:09.959
We must go and talk to Toad before it's too late.

00:19:10.019 --> 00:19:11.880
Good, says Rat.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.631
We must save poor Toad.

00:19:14.691 --> 00:19:20.834
When they arrive at Toad Hall, a big red car is in front of the house.

00:19:20.894 --> 00:19:23.980
Toad is coming out of the house.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:30.238
He is wearing goggles, a cap, an enormous coat, and gloves.

00:19:30.298 --> 00:19:33.650
Hello, he says when he sees them.

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:38.972
Take them inside, says Badger to Rat and Mole.

00:19:39.032 --> 00:19:41.494
They take him inside.

00:19:41.554 --> 00:19:44.135
Now, Toad, says Badger.

00:19:44.195 --> 00:19:46.996
Take these stupid clothes off.

00:19:47.056 --> 00:19:48.937
No, says Toad.

00:19:48.997 --> 00:19:50.928
Why are you doing this?

00:19:50.988 --> 00:19:52.288
Take his clothes off.

00:19:52.348 --> 00:19:53.938
Badger orders.

00:19:53.998 --> 00:20:00.989
Rat sits on Toad, and mold takes off Toad's motor clothes.

00:20:01.049 --> 00:20:07.982
Now, Toad says, Badger, you don't listen to our advice.

00:20:08.042 --> 00:20:17.436
You're spending all your money, and people are talking about the animals because of your fast driving and problems with the police.

00:20:17.496 --> 00:20:20.347
But Toad is not sorry.

00:20:20.407 --> 00:20:22.990
So they lock him in a bedroom.

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:27.032
You can come out when you're sorry," says Rat.

00:20:27.092 --> 00:20:29.744
They go downstairs.

00:20:29.804 --> 00:20:32.885
Toad shouts at them through the keyhole.

00:20:32.945 --> 00:20:36.967
Toad's very determined, says Badger.

00:20:37.027 --> 00:20:39.278
It's a difficult situation.

00:20:39.338 --> 00:20:43.350
We must never leave Toad alone.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:49.092
The day's pass, but Toad is still interested in cars.

00:20:49.152 --> 00:20:51.746
He becomes depressed.

00:20:51.807 --> 00:20:55.410
One morning Rat is with Toad.

00:20:55.471 --> 00:20:57.561
How are you today, Toad?

00:20:57.621 --> 00:20:58.631
He asks.

00:20:58.691 --> 00:21:00.892
Not very well.

00:21:00.952 --> 00:21:02.572
Reply, Toad.

00:21:02.632 --> 00:21:06.983
Could you go to the village and call the doctor?

00:21:07.043 --> 00:21:09.043
Rat is worried.

00:21:09.103 --> 00:21:10.493
A doctor?

00:21:10.553 --> 00:21:13.494
He must be very ill.

00:21:13.554 --> 00:21:17.274
He goes out of the room and locks the door.

00:21:17.334 --> 00:21:20.256
Then he runs to the village.

00:21:20.316 --> 00:21:23.079
Toad jumps out of bed and laughs.

00:21:23.099 --> 00:21:25.870
He gets dressed quickly.

00:21:25.931 --> 00:21:28.472
He puts some money in his pockets.

00:21:28.532 --> 00:21:32.386
He climbs out of the window and jumps to the ground.

00:21:32.446 --> 00:21:37.518
He then walks away in the opposite direction to Rat.

00:21:37.578 --> 00:21:39.890
The sun is shining.

00:21:39.951 --> 00:21:43.333
And he is very happy with himself.

00:21:43.393 --> 00:21:46.155
Poor Ratty thinks.

00:21:46.215 --> 00:21:49.967
He's a very good animal, but not very intelligent.

00:21:50.027 --> 00:21:52.308
I must educate him one day."

00:21:52.368 --> 00:21:58.582
He arrives in a small town and sees a sign, the red lion.

00:21:58.643 --> 00:22:00.974
Toad is very hungry.

00:22:01.034 --> 00:22:05.376
He goes into the inn and orders a big lunch.

00:22:05.436 --> 00:22:12.422
Suddenly he hears, FUP, FUP, and sees a car outside the inn.

00:22:12.482 --> 00:22:15.890
The people get out and go into the inn.

00:22:15.950 --> 00:22:18.730
Toad walks outside.

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:21.322
He looks at the car.

00:22:21.382 --> 00:22:28.880
I wonder, he thinks, if this type of car starts easily.

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:34.806
In a dream, he starts the car.

00:22:34.866 --> 00:22:43.844
Then sits in the driver's seat and drives away.

00:22:43.904 --> 00:22:49.140
He doesn't think about right or wrong.

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:55.089
He drives faster and faster.

00:22:55.149 --> 00:23:02.367
We must punish this villain severely," says the magistrate.

00:23:02.427 --> 00:23:12.086
His guilty, first of all, of stealing a motorcar, and secondly of driving dangerously, and thirdly of being rude to the police.

00:23:12.106 --> 00:23:17.050
I give you twenty years in prison.

00:23:17.110 --> 00:23:29.307
Poor Toad is locked up in prison.

00:23:29.367 --> 00:23:53.904
Chapter 6 Toad's Adventures Toad is very unhappy.

00:23:53.964 --> 00:24:00.631
This is the end of everything, he thinks.

00:24:00.691 --> 00:24:03.949
The end of the career of Toad.

00:24:04.009 --> 00:24:06.751
The popular and handsome Toad.

00:24:06.811 --> 00:24:10.234
The rich and kind Toad.

00:24:10.294 --> 00:24:13.406
He starts crying.

00:24:13.466 --> 00:24:18.339
Now I must stay in this dark prison.

00:24:18.399 --> 00:24:49.722
who clever rat and sensible mole intelligent badger poor toad the days and weeks pass and he refuses to eat the jailer has got a daughter and she helps her father in the print she is very fond of animals and is sorry for toad One day, she asks.

00:24:49.782 --> 00:24:53.035
Father, please let me look after Toad.

00:24:53.095 --> 00:24:56.398
He's so unhappy and so thin.

00:24:56.458 --> 00:25:00.481
She knocks on the door of Toad's cell.

00:25:00.541 --> 00:25:02.944
Now, Toad.

00:25:03.004 --> 00:25:04.014
She says.

00:25:04.074 --> 00:25:06.476
Sit up and stop crying.

00:25:06.537 --> 00:25:09.389
Be sensible and eat some dinner.

00:25:09.449 --> 00:25:12.562
The dinner smells very good.

00:25:12.622 --> 00:25:16.825
And Toad starts to think that life is not so bad.

00:25:16.885 --> 00:25:20.256
He sits up and starts to eat.

00:25:20.316 --> 00:25:24.556
The jailer's daughter asks him about Toad Hall.

00:25:24.616 --> 00:25:27.557
He talks about his home.

00:25:27.617 --> 00:25:31.818
Then she asks him about his animal friends.

00:25:31.878 --> 00:25:36.029
When the girl leaves, Toad is himself again.

00:25:36.089 --> 00:25:40.100
The same, arrogant animal.

00:25:40.160 --> 00:25:46.010
The days pass and they have a lot of interesting talks together.

00:25:46.070 --> 00:25:52.900
The jailer's daughter is very sorry for Toad, and thinks it is wrong that Toad is in prison.

00:25:52.960 --> 00:26:02.965
Vayne Toad believes that she is in love with him, and is a little sorry that the social gap between them is so big.

00:26:03.025 --> 00:26:08.312
One morning she says, Listen Toad, I've got an aunt.

00:26:08.372 --> 00:26:12.594
She's a washer woman and does the washing for all the prisoners here.

00:26:12.654 --> 00:26:17.176
Now, you're very rich and she's very poor.

00:26:17.236 --> 00:26:23.800
I think that if you pay her, she can give you her dress and bonnet and you can escape.

00:26:23.860 --> 00:26:25.610
You are very similar.

00:26:25.671 --> 00:26:28.692
We are not, says Toad.

00:26:28.752 --> 00:26:32.064
I'm very elegant, considering I'm a Toad.

00:26:32.124 --> 00:26:35.655
My aunt's also elegant, considering she's a washer woman.

00:26:35.715 --> 00:26:36.865
Says the girl.

00:26:36.925 --> 00:26:41.486
I'm trying to help you, and you are proud and ungrateful.

00:26:41.546 --> 00:26:45.917
Please introduce me to your aunt, says Toad.

00:26:45.977 --> 00:26:50.928
The next evening, the girl's aunt comes into the cell.

00:26:50.988 --> 00:26:54.009
She is carrying Toad's washing.

00:26:54.069 --> 00:26:58.398
On the table is a pile of gold coins.

00:26:58.458 --> 00:27:04.647
The washer woman gives Toad a cotton dress, an apron, and a bite.

00:27:04.707 --> 00:27:11.410
Then Toad takes off his coat and waistcoat and puts on the dress apron and bonnet.

00:27:11.470 --> 00:27:13.290
Goodbye Toad!

00:27:13.350 --> 00:27:15.011
Says the girl.

00:27:15.071 --> 00:27:19.212
Toad is nervous, but he goes out.

00:27:19.272 --> 00:27:21.703
No one stops him.

00:27:21.764 --> 00:27:26.196
When he is outside, he walks towards the town.

00:27:26.257 --> 00:27:33.432
Soon he sees some red and green lights and the noise of a train.

00:27:33.492 --> 00:27:36.713
Ah-ha!

00:27:36.773 --> 00:27:39.155
He thinks a railway station.

00:27:39.215 --> 00:27:42.296
I can catch a train home.

00:27:42.356 --> 00:27:48.750
He goes to the ticket office and asks for a ticket to the village near Toad Hall.

00:27:48.810 --> 00:27:51.371
But he has no money.

00:27:51.431 --> 00:27:55.294
It is all in his waistcoat pocket in the prison.

00:27:55.354 --> 00:27:58.256
He cannot get home.

00:27:58.316 --> 00:28:01.068
Toad is very sad.

00:28:01.128 --> 00:28:03.792
He walks down the platform.

00:28:03.852 --> 00:28:05.823
He starts to cry.

00:28:05.843 --> 00:28:08.986
Hello!

00:28:09.046 --> 00:28:10.337
Watch the matter!

00:28:10.397 --> 00:28:12.088
asks the train driver.

00:28:12.108 --> 00:28:13.730
Oh, sir!

00:28:13.790 --> 00:28:15.178
cries Toad.

00:28:15.238 --> 00:28:18.206
I'm a poor washer woman.

00:28:18.266 --> 00:28:19.917
I have no money.

00:28:19.977 --> 00:28:23.909
I can't pay for the ticket in their Musket home tonight.

00:28:23.969 --> 00:28:27.991
Very well, says the kind train driver.

00:28:28.051 --> 00:28:29.702
You're the washer woman.

00:28:29.762 --> 00:28:33.544
I can give you a ride if you wash some shirts for me.

00:28:33.604 --> 00:28:35.614
Toad climbs up.

00:28:35.674 --> 00:28:40.976
The guard waves his flag and the train moves out of the station.

00:28:41.036 --> 00:28:44.376
Now Toad is very happy.

00:28:44.436 --> 00:28:50.608
He thinks about Toad Hall, his friends, and good things to eat.

00:28:50.668 --> 00:29:00.670
After some time, the train driver says, It's very strange with the last train tonight, but I'm sure there's another train behind us.

00:29:00.730 --> 00:29:04.927
Toad immediately becomes serious and depressed.

00:29:04.987 --> 00:29:08.378
And the train is full of policemen with truncheons!

00:29:08.438 --> 00:29:09.420
They're shouting!

00:29:09.480 --> 00:29:10.221
Stop!

00:29:10.281 --> 00:29:10.962
Stop!

00:29:11.022 --> 00:29:11.773
Stop!

00:29:11.833 --> 00:29:14.427
Continue the train driver.

00:29:14.487 --> 00:29:17.734
Toad falls to his knees.

00:29:17.794 --> 00:29:20.565
Save me, Mr. Train Driver.

00:29:20.625 --> 00:29:22.266
I'm not a washerwoman.

00:29:22.326 --> 00:29:24.146
I'm toad.

00:29:24.206 --> 00:29:27.337
The well-known and popular, Mr. Toad.

00:29:27.397 --> 00:29:28.627
They want me.

00:29:28.687 --> 00:29:31.747
I'm a car thief, and I'm running away from prison.

00:29:31.807 --> 00:29:35.278
The train driver looks very serious.

00:29:35.338 --> 00:29:38.348
I must stop and give you to the police.

00:29:38.408 --> 00:29:40.809
But you're obviously very sorry.

00:29:40.869 --> 00:29:42.749
Soon, there's a tunnel.

00:29:42.809 --> 00:29:44.860
At the other end, there's a wood.

00:29:44.920 --> 00:29:48.147
You must jump out and hide in the wood.

00:29:48.207 --> 00:29:51.215
After the tunnel, Toad jumps.

00:29:51.275 --> 00:29:54.216
He runs into the wood and hides.

00:29:54.276 --> 00:30:00.338
The police train comes out of the tunnel and continues following the other train.

00:30:00.398 --> 00:30:05.950
Toad laughs, but soon he stops laughing.

00:30:06.010 --> 00:30:10.561
It is very late and dark and cold.

00:30:10.621 --> 00:30:16.722
He is in a strange wood with no money and far away from friends and home.

00:30:16.782 --> 00:30:32.762
Cold, hungry and tired, he makes a bed with dead leaves and branches under a tree, and goes to sleep.

00:30:32.822 --> 00:30:50.652
Chapter 7 The Further Adventures of Toad Toad wakes up early.

00:30:50.712 --> 00:30:53.374
The sun is shining.

00:30:53.434 --> 00:30:57.516
He stands up and starts walking.

00:30:57.577 --> 00:31:00.588
Soon he sees a canal.

00:31:00.648 --> 00:31:04.380
On it there is a barge pulled by a horse.

00:31:04.440 --> 00:31:07.052
There is a woman on the barge.

00:31:07.112 --> 00:31:10.174
Good morning, she says to Toad.

00:31:10.234 --> 00:31:13.288
Maybe it's good for you, says Toad.

00:31:13.348 --> 00:31:19.684
Then I'm a poor water woman, and I'm going to see my married daughter.

00:31:19.744 --> 00:31:21.356
She's in trouble.

00:31:21.416 --> 00:31:24.007
All of my other children are alone.

00:31:24.027 --> 00:31:26.769
I'm lost with no money.

00:31:26.789 --> 00:31:28.760
Oh, where does your daughter live?

00:31:28.820 --> 00:31:30.521
asks the barge woman.

00:31:30.581 --> 00:31:33.383
Neither with her replies toed.

00:31:33.443 --> 00:31:37.265
Near a fine house called Toad Hall.

00:31:37.325 --> 00:31:38.466
Toad Hall?

00:31:38.526 --> 00:31:40.347
I'm going in that direction.

00:31:40.407 --> 00:31:41.579
Says the woman.

00:31:41.639 --> 00:31:45.673
Come with me in the barge, I can take you near Toad Hall.

00:31:45.734 --> 00:31:48.766
Lucky Toad gets onto the barge.

00:31:48.827 --> 00:31:51.570
So, you're a washer woman.

00:31:51.630 --> 00:31:52.880
Asks the woman.

00:31:52.940 --> 00:31:55.183
Oh yes, says Toad.

00:31:55.243 --> 00:31:57.555
The best in the country, I'm pretty good.

00:31:57.575 --> 00:31:59.237
I love watching.

00:31:59.257 --> 00:32:02.460
More than I'm very lucky meeting you.

00:32:02.520 --> 00:32:03.748
Says the woman.

00:32:03.808 --> 00:32:07.598
I like washing too, but I never have the time.

00:32:07.618 --> 00:32:10.680
There's a big pile of washing inside.

00:32:10.740 --> 00:32:12.982
You can do my washing.

00:32:13.042 --> 00:32:14.683
Toad is frightened.

00:32:14.703 --> 00:32:15.763
Oh no!

00:32:15.823 --> 00:32:17.794
I didn't want to ruin your clothes.

00:32:17.854 --> 00:32:20.756
I usually wash gently these clothes.

00:32:20.817 --> 00:32:22.017
Oh no!

00:32:22.077 --> 00:32:23.308
says the woman.

00:32:23.368 --> 00:32:25.900
I want you to be happy.

00:32:25.960 --> 00:32:31.923
Toad is worried, but he thinks it can't be so difficult to wash.

00:32:31.982 --> 00:32:36.114
Half an hour later Toad is angry.

00:32:36.174 --> 00:32:38.846
The clothes are still dirty.

00:32:38.906 --> 00:32:41.668
Suddenly he hears the barge woman.

00:32:41.729 --> 00:32:43.850
She is laughing.

00:32:43.910 --> 00:32:46.212
You can't wash.

00:32:46.272 --> 00:32:48.183
You aren't a washer woman.

00:32:48.243 --> 00:32:50.315
Toad is furious.

00:32:50.375 --> 00:32:53.187
You common barge woman.

00:32:53.247 --> 00:32:54.908
I'm Toad.

00:32:54.928 --> 00:32:57.950
The distinguished Toad.

00:32:58.010 --> 00:33:00.339
You mustn't laugh at me.

00:33:00.399 --> 00:33:04.137
The woman looks at Toad under his bonnet.

00:33:04.197 --> 00:33:05.768
Yes, you are.

00:33:05.828 --> 00:33:06.568
She cries.

00:33:06.588 --> 00:33:11.460
A horrible Toad in my nice clean barge.

00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:17.962
She takes him by the legs and throws him into the water.

00:33:18.022 --> 00:33:20.744
It is very cold.

00:33:20.804 --> 00:33:23.505
Toad gets out of the water.

00:33:23.565 --> 00:33:25.826
He looks at the woman.

00:33:25.886 --> 00:33:28.877
She is laughing at him.

00:33:28.937 --> 00:33:31.728
Toad wants revenge.

00:33:31.788 --> 00:33:34.168
He runs after the barge.

00:33:34.229 --> 00:33:37.810
He takes the horse and gallops away.

00:33:37.870 --> 00:33:39.100
Stop!

00:33:39.160 --> 00:33:40.260
Stop!

00:33:40.320 --> 00:33:41.341
Stop!

00:33:41.401 --> 00:33:43.251
Shouts the woman.

00:33:43.311 --> 00:33:47.632
Toad laughs.

00:33:47.692 --> 00:33:56.840
After some miles, Toad and the horse are sleepy, and the horse stops to eat some grass.

00:33:56.900 --> 00:33:59.346
Toad looks around.

00:33:59.406 --> 00:34:03.866
He sees an old dirty gypsy caravan.

00:34:03.926 --> 00:34:06.867
There is a man sitting next to it.

00:34:06.927 --> 00:34:10.128
There is also a fire.

00:34:10.188 --> 00:34:15.409
Over the fire is a pot full of stew.

00:34:15.470 --> 00:34:22.334
Toad is very hungry, and the stew smells delicious.

00:34:22.395 --> 00:34:26.539
The gypsy asks, do you want to say your horse?

00:34:26.599 --> 00:34:29.270
No, no, replies toad.

00:34:29.330 --> 00:34:31.430
I love my horse.

00:34:31.491 --> 00:34:34.241
But how much can you pay me?

00:34:34.301 --> 00:34:36.972
A shilling a leg replies the gypsy.

00:34:36.992 --> 00:34:41.304
My shilling a leg says toad.

00:34:41.364 --> 00:34:45.044
I must work out how much that is in total.

00:34:45.104 --> 00:34:47.697
He thinks for a minute.

00:34:47.758 --> 00:34:52.263
But that only for shillings, I cannot accept that.

00:34:52.323 --> 00:34:57.698
Give me six shillings and some breakfast and you can have my horse."

00:34:57.758 --> 00:35:02.882
The gypsy agrees and gives Toad six shillings.

00:35:02.942 --> 00:35:08.066
Then he gives him an enormous plate of stew.

00:35:08.126 --> 00:35:13.372
Toad eats and eats and eats.

00:35:13.432 --> 00:35:20.098
After the gypsy gives him directions for the riverbank and Toad says goodbye.

00:35:20.158 --> 00:35:23.250
He is happy again.

00:35:23.310 --> 00:35:25.570
The sun is shining.

00:35:25.630 --> 00:35:30.933
He has money in his pockets and a full stock.

00:35:30.953 --> 00:35:33.824
And he is near home.

00:35:33.884 --> 00:35:38.644
After some time he sees a car in the distance.

00:35:38.705 --> 00:35:41.414
One before thinks Toad.

00:35:41.474 --> 00:35:44.685
I can stop the car and ask for a lift.

00:35:44.745 --> 00:35:48.626
Then I can return to Toad Hall in a car.

00:35:48.686 --> 00:35:53.608
He steps into the road and the car slows down.

00:35:53.668 --> 00:35:59.520
But suddenly Toad becomes pale and falls to the ground.

00:35:59.580 --> 00:36:07.240
It is the car from outside the red lion and the people in the car are the same people.

00:36:07.300 --> 00:36:08.798
Oh no!

00:36:08.858 --> 00:36:10.419
Prison again!

00:36:10.439 --> 00:36:15.022
Dry bread and water again!

00:36:15.082 --> 00:36:18.234
What a fool I am!

00:36:18.294 --> 00:36:20.464
Tries toad!

00:36:20.524 --> 00:36:23.186
The car stops.

00:36:23.246 --> 00:36:26.018
And two men get out.

00:36:26.078 --> 00:36:27.729
Oh dear!

00:36:27.789 --> 00:36:29.970
A washer woman in the road!

00:36:30.031 --> 00:36:32.632
Let's take her to the village!

00:36:32.692 --> 00:36:38.106
They put toad in the car and continue along the road.

00:36:38.167 --> 00:36:43.521
Toad feels brave again, because the men do not recognise him.

00:36:43.581 --> 00:36:45.872
How do you feel now?

00:36:45.932 --> 00:36:47.904
asks one of the men.

00:36:47.964 --> 00:36:51.616
Better, thank you sir, says Toad.

00:36:51.676 --> 00:36:59.722
But maybe, if I can sit in the front seat next to the driver, I can have some fresh air on my face.

00:36:59.782 --> 00:37:02.803
Very sensible, says the man.

00:37:02.863 --> 00:37:06.654
So Toad gets into the front seat.

00:37:06.714 --> 00:37:09.275
Please, sir, says Toad.

00:37:09.335 --> 00:37:11.846
Can I drive the car for a little?

00:37:11.906 --> 00:37:14.466
The driver laughs.

00:37:14.526 --> 00:37:17.938
You can try, madam.

00:37:17.998 --> 00:37:24.220
Toad gets into the driver's seat and pretends to listen to the driver's instructions.

00:37:24.280 --> 00:37:27.411
At first he drives very carefully.

00:37:27.471 --> 00:37:30.816
The two men laugh and applaud.

00:37:30.876 --> 00:37:36.152
Just imagine a washer woman driving so well.

00:37:36.212 --> 00:37:43.294
Toad goes a little faster, then faster and faster.

00:37:43.354 --> 00:37:47.986
The men say, be careful washer woman.

00:37:48.046 --> 00:37:52.969
This annoys Toad, and he loses his head.

00:37:53.029 --> 00:37:54.860
What a woman!

00:37:54.920 --> 00:37:56.221
He shouts.

00:37:56.281 --> 00:38:02.597
and told the motor-car thief, the famous, the clever, the fearless Toad.

00:38:02.657 --> 00:38:09.362
The two men jump on Toad and the car goes off the road and finishes up in a pond.

00:38:09.422 --> 00:38:15.646
Toad flies through the air and lands on the soft grass of a meadow.

00:38:15.706 --> 00:38:20.764
He gets up and starts to run.

00:38:20.824 --> 00:38:27.140
He cries, Toad wins again, clever Toad.

00:38:27.200 --> 00:38:29.370
He looks behind him.

00:38:29.430 --> 00:38:34.522
He sees the driver and two policemen running after him.

00:38:34.582 --> 00:38:36.954
What an idiot I am!

00:38:37.014 --> 00:38:39.094
He cries while he runs.

00:38:39.154 --> 00:38:42.176
How stupid I am!

00:38:42.236 --> 00:38:47.956
He runs and runs, but they get nearer.

00:38:48.016 --> 00:38:50.515
Paul towed.

00:38:50.575 --> 00:38:54.757
He is a fat animal and his legs are short.

00:38:54.817 --> 00:38:58.179
Suddenly he falls into water.

00:38:58.239 --> 00:39:00.670
He is in the river.

00:39:00.730 --> 00:39:06.694
The water carries him along and soon he sees a big hole in the river bank.

00:39:06.754 --> 00:39:12.752
He takes hold and pulls himself out of the water.

00:39:12.812 --> 00:39:21.031
He looks into the hole and sees a familiar face brown and small.

00:39:21.091 --> 00:39:24.182
It is the water rat.

00:39:24.242 --> 00:39:30.336
Toad tries to tell Rat about his adventures and about how clever he is.

00:39:30.396 --> 00:39:33.267
But Rat is very serious.

00:39:33.327 --> 00:39:35.918
Toad, you are very silly.

00:39:35.978 --> 00:39:40.751
You must try to be sensible and mustn't embarrass your friends.

00:39:40.811 --> 00:39:43.322
Toad is very sorry.

00:39:43.382 --> 00:39:45.744
You're right, Ratty," he says.

00:39:45.804 --> 00:39:48.218
I want to be a good toad in the future.

00:39:48.278 --> 00:39:53.745
Let's have coffee, and then I can go to Toad Hall and get some clean clothes.

00:39:53.805 --> 00:39:56.458
Go to Toad Hall, tries Rat.

00:39:56.518 --> 00:39:59.734
Don't you know Toad becomes pale.

00:39:59.794 --> 00:40:02.338
No, what, Ratty?

00:40:02.398 --> 00:40:05.340
You don't know about the ferrets and the weasels.

00:40:05.400 --> 00:40:07.630
They're living in Toad Hall.

00:40:07.690 --> 00:40:10.352
They think you aren't coming back from prison.

00:40:10.412 --> 00:40:14.794
They lie in bed half the day and eat your food and drink your drink.

00:40:14.854 --> 00:40:16.925
The place is in a mess.

00:40:16.985 --> 00:40:19.706
Toad gets up and takes a stick.

00:40:19.766 --> 00:40:22.258
It's no good, says Rat.

00:40:22.318 --> 00:40:25.029
They've got centuries and are armed.

00:40:25.089 --> 00:40:26.440
You must wait.

00:40:26.500 --> 00:40:29.062
But Toad doesn't want to wait.

00:40:29.122 --> 00:40:32.684
He marches down the road to Toad Hall.

00:40:32.744 --> 00:40:35.415
At the front gate there is a ferret.

00:40:35.475 --> 00:40:40.327
He shoots at Toad, and so Toad runs back to Rat.

00:40:40.387 --> 00:40:43.098
Badger and Mole arrive.

00:40:43.158 --> 00:40:46.548
We can't attack the house, says Badger.

00:40:46.609 --> 00:40:50.412
They're too strong, but there's a tunnel.

00:40:50.472 --> 00:40:54.445
It goes from the riverbank to the middle of Toad Hall.

00:40:54.505 --> 00:41:00.720
Tomorrow night, it's the Chief Wiesel's birthday, and there's a big party in the dining room.

00:41:00.781 --> 00:41:06.606
We can enter secretly and then run into the dining room with our pistols and swords.

00:41:06.666 --> 00:41:08.828
Yes, yes!"

00:41:08.888 --> 00:41:10.900
cries Toad happily.

00:41:10.960 --> 00:41:15.292
Now, it's time to go to bed, says Badger.

00:41:15.352 --> 00:41:25.455
We must rest, because we've got a lot of work to do tomorrow night.

00:41:25.515 --> 00:41:50.712
Chapter 8 The Return of Mr. Toad The following evening, Rat calls everyone into the sitting room and prepares them for the expedition.

00:41:50.772 --> 00:42:00.380
He gives them a belt, a sword, a pair of pistols, a policeman's truncheon, handcuffs, a flask, and a sandwich box.

00:42:00.440 --> 00:42:10.693
When they are ready, Badger takes a lantern and says, Now, follow me, Mole first, then Rat and Toad last.

00:42:10.753 --> 00:42:14.084
And Toady, don't talk.

00:42:14.145 --> 00:42:19.677
Toad wants to be part of the expedition, so he is quiet.

00:42:19.737 --> 00:42:26.730
Badger takes them along the river for a little way, and then goes into a hole in the riverbank.

00:42:26.790 --> 00:42:29.964
Mole and Rat follow silently.

00:42:30.024 --> 00:42:35.488
But Toad slips and falls into the water with a loud splash.

00:42:35.548 --> 00:42:41.120
His friends pull him out, but Badger is very angry.

00:42:41.180 --> 00:42:44.691
They continue along the secret tunnel.

00:42:44.751 --> 00:42:54.934
It is cold and dark, and poor Toad starts to shiver because he is frightened, and also because he is completely wet.

00:42:54.994 --> 00:43:00.184
At last Badger says, we must be under the hall now.

00:43:00.245 --> 00:43:03.225
They are at the end of the tunnel.

00:43:03.285 --> 00:43:07.206
There is a door, and they all push against it.

00:43:07.266 --> 00:43:12.318
It opens, and they are in the pantry next to the dining room.

00:43:12.378 --> 00:43:15.804
The weasels are making a lot of noise.

00:43:15.864 --> 00:43:20.460
They hear the Chief Wiesel say, Thank you, thank you.

00:43:20.520 --> 00:43:27.743
But before I finish, I would like to say one word about our kind host, Mr Toad.

00:43:27.803 --> 00:43:32.315
Good, modest, honest Toad.

00:43:32.375 --> 00:43:37.327
Everybody laughs, and Toad is furious.

00:43:37.387 --> 00:43:45.020
Badger stands up, takes his stick and says, The time is come, follow me.

00:43:45.080 --> 00:43:50.822
They open the door, and the four friends run into the dining room.

00:43:50.882 --> 00:43:56.204
The weasels and ferrets are terrified and run everywhere in a panic.

00:43:56.264 --> 00:44:07.830
The four friends go up and down the room, hitting the animals with their sticks, and the weasels and ferrets try to escape through the windows and up the chimney.

00:44:07.890 --> 00:44:12.516
After five minutes, the room is empty.

00:44:12.576 --> 00:44:18.173
Now Toad says Badger, we've got your house back for you.

00:44:18.233 --> 00:44:20.935
Now you can get us some food.

00:44:20.995 --> 00:44:22.866
I'm hungry.

00:44:22.926 --> 00:44:31.101
Toad is a little offended because Badger doesn't tell him, well done, and you are a great fighter.

00:44:31.161 --> 00:44:36.404
But he says nothing and finds some food for them to eat.

00:44:36.464 --> 00:44:42.909
The next morning Toad wakes up late as usual.

00:44:42.970 --> 00:44:47.364
He comes down for breakfast.

00:44:47.424 --> 00:44:54.647
Rat and Mole are sitting in the garden, and Badger is in the armchair, reading the newspaper.

00:44:54.707 --> 00:44:57.348
Told, says Badger.

00:44:57.408 --> 00:45:04.052
You must have a banquet to celebrate your return, and you must write the invitations now.

00:45:04.112 --> 00:45:04.932
What?

00:45:04.992 --> 00:45:06.303
cries Toad.

00:45:06.363 --> 00:45:11.800
I must stay inside and write letters on a lovely morning like this.

00:45:11.860 --> 00:45:14.756
But then Toad has an idea.

00:45:14.816 --> 00:45:15.847
But wait!

00:45:15.907 --> 00:45:19.698
Of course, dear Badger, I can start immediately!

00:45:19.758 --> 00:45:26.562
Toad wants to write about his important part in the fight and also about his many adventures.

00:45:26.622 --> 00:45:32.397
He also thinks he can give a speech and sing some songs at the banquet.

00:45:32.457 --> 00:45:44.315
He works hard all morning, and when a weasel knocks at the door at midday and asks if he can be of service, Toad tells him to deliver the invitations.

00:45:44.375 --> 00:45:49.911
But after lunch, Rat and Badger sit Toad in a chair.

00:45:49.971 --> 00:45:53.211
Look, Toad, says Rat.

00:45:53.271 --> 00:45:55.401
You must understand.

00:45:55.461 --> 00:45:59.712
You can't give a speech or sing songs.

00:45:59.772 --> 00:46:03.013
Can't I sing just one little song?

00:46:03.073 --> 00:46:04.554
asks Toad.

00:46:04.614 --> 00:46:06.834
No, says Rat.

00:46:06.894 --> 00:46:14.828
You know that your songs are all boasting and vanity, and your speeches are gross exaggeration.

00:46:14.888 --> 00:46:17.961
You know you must change.

00:46:18.021 --> 00:46:19.132
You're right.

00:46:19.192 --> 00:46:21.984
I promise to be a different Toad.

00:46:22.044 --> 00:46:25.295
But this is a hard world.

00:46:25.356 --> 00:46:31.730
That evening when the banquet begins, Toad enters the dining room to meet his guests.

00:46:31.790 --> 00:46:34.952
All the animals cheer and congratulate him.

00:46:35.012 --> 00:46:37.784
But Toad is very humble.

00:46:37.844 --> 00:46:40.285
Oh no, he says.

00:46:40.345 --> 00:46:44.758
Badger, Rat and Mole are the real heroes.

00:46:44.818 --> 00:46:53.850
The animals are very puzzled by his behavior, and Toad is happy because he feels that everyone is very interested in him.

00:46:53.910 --> 00:47:01.784
At the end of the evening, some animals ask for a speech and a song, but Toad shakes his head.

00:47:01.844 --> 00:47:05.825
He is a changed Toad.

00:47:05.885 --> 00:47:13.969
After this great adventure, the four animals continue their lives in joy and contentment.

00:47:14.029 --> 00:47:22.352
Toad sends a gold chain and lock it with pearls to the jailer's daughter with a modest and grateful letter.

00:47:22.412 --> 00:47:33.234
The train driver also receives thanks and compensation, and Badger also makes Toad send money to the Bardwoman for her horse.

00:47:33.294 --> 00:47:40.316
Sometimes during the long summer evenings, the friends go for a walk in the Wildwood.

00:47:40.376 --> 00:47:43.525
The weasels greet them with respect.

00:47:43.585 --> 00:47:48.036
Mother weasels call their children point and say, Look!

00:47:48.096 --> 00:47:55.831
There goes great Mr Toad, the brave rat and famous Mr Mole!

00:47:55.891 --> 00:48:06.488
But when their children are naughty, they say that the terrible grey badger is coming to get them.

00:48:06.548 --> 00:48:15.873
This is of course not true, because badger is very fond of children But it always has an effect.

